  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Carried Away (Carl Broemel song)** (1 review): Intro occurs during Heartbreakin Man, causing Carried Away to start without its intro [7]\n- Listener assumes this song and Steam Engine are intertwined due to duration [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Picture of You**: back after 106 archived shows (2084 days) [8]\n- **Hopefully-I Will Be There When You Die**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [8]\n- **Isn't It a Pity (George Harrison cover)**: rare: 6 archived performances; with Iron & Wine [8]\n- **Rock the Casbah (The Clash cover)**: rare: 4 archived performances [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **MMJ2012-09-12.MMJ-Wiltern-9-12-12** (recommended): source not stated; 21 songs; 139 min; rated 3.83/5 by 6 [1]. Said about its sound: Listener confirms the recording sounds great despite numbering confusion; Listener notes tracking issues at the end of track seven and start of nine [3][4]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Guests: Iron & Wine [1]\n- Listener describes the three-night run as truly unforgettable [5]\n- Recorded at back of third terrace, directly in front of SBD and board [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **MMJ2012-09-12.MMJ-Wiltern-9-12-12**: taped by Pat Myers; transferred by Pat Myers; source: Neumann SKM-140'sGrace V3-Dr-680 [1]. Also: Source files were deleted to free up space for other material [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by @brahbrahbrah: [SETLIST: My Morning Jacket @ The Wiltern, Los Angeles, CA 9/12/12 - Live Music Blog](https://livemusicblog.com/setlist-my-morning-jacket-the-wiltern-los-angeles-ca-91212/) [9]",
